Burn severity from {{ sensor }} surface reflectance served by {{ provider }}
(STAC collection {{ collection }}).

For each window (prefire {{ prefire[0] }} to {{ prefire[1] }}, postfire
{{ postfire[0] }} to {{ postfire[1] }}), every scene covering the area is used,
except that where a provider lists one Sentinel-2 acquisition under several
processings, only the newest processing baseline is kept.

Each scene's NIR ({{ bands.nir }}) and SWIR ({{ bands.swir }}) digital numbers
are converted to reflectance with that scene's own published scale and offset
(reflectance = DN x scale + offset). Observations whose NIR or SWIR reflectance
is not above 0 (which includes the products' nodata), or that are flagged in the
{{ bands.mask }} band ({{ mask_description }}), are excluded, and
the per-pixel {{ composite }} of the remaining observations forms each window's
composite.

Scenes are read with {{ resampling }}-neighbour resampling onto a
{{ "%g" | format(resolution) }} m grid in EPSG:{{ epsg }}, aligned to the
sensor's native pixels.

NBR = (NIR - SWIR) / (NIR + SWIR) per composite; dNBR, RdNBR and RBR follow,
each asset carrying its formula in processing:expression. Pixels with no clear
observation in either window are nodata (-9999).

The scenes used, with their processing baselines and offsets, are listed in
fire:prefire_scenes and fire:postfire_scenes. Pipeline version
{{ pipeline_version }}.
